#Requires -Version 5.1
<#
.SYNOPSIS
    Generates an interactive HTML hierarchy report of all NinjaOne policies,
    device assignments, and per-device policy section overrides — using the
    NinjaOne REST API directly with no PowerShell module required.
 
.DESCRIPTION
    Map-NinjaOnePolicies.ps1 authenticates against the NinjaOne REST API v2
    using OAuth2 Client Credentials, then collects policies, devices,
    organisations, locations, and per-device policy section overrides.
 
    A WinForms GUI prompts for API credentials and region on launch, then
    presents a policy exclusion picker before generating the report.
 
    Output includes:
      - A dark-mode interactive HTML report with a collapsible policy tree,
        per-policy device counts (total / inherited / assigned / stale /
        overrides), colour-coded node class badges, live search, Hide Unused
        toggle, and a full per-device overrides table.
      - PolicyReport.csv    — one row per policy with all device statistics.
      - PolicyOverrides.csv — one row per device that has section overrides,
        listing the overridden section names.
 
    Compatible with all NinjaOne regions: US, US2, EU, OC, CA.
    Requires PowerShell 5.1 or later. No third-party modules needed.
 
.NOTES
    Author  : Spencer A. Heath
    Version : 2.0
    GitHub  : https://github.com/SpencerAHeath
 
